        "node_id": "n_5_cff08b",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error in the previous solution was due to an incorrect interpretation of the problem. The maximum number of targets that can be destroyed is not necessarily the sum of the maximum targets in any row and column, but rather the sum of the maximum targets in any row and column, minus 1 if there's an intersection. This reasoning step should be replaced with:\n\nFind the row and column with the maximum sum of targets, and then check if there's an intersection. If there is, we need to subtract 1 from the total to avoid double-counting the intersecting target.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-3105491540031284130",
